    "body": "Proof of the defect, before the fix (commit `3c7385fba`):\n\n- The test `default_machine_missing` copies the `camcraft-cli` exe into a temp folder. The folder has `assets/posts` and an `assets/machines` folder with no `3axis-vmc.mch`, or with a malformed file (`{ \"kinematics\": `).\n- `camcraft-cli process job.camproj -o out.nc` exits 0 in the two cases. It writes a complete Fanuc program: `%`, `O0001 (CAMCRAFT)`, `G21`, `G90 G54 G40 G49 G80`, `T01 M6`, `G43 H01`, `S12000 M3`, the facing passes, `M5`, `G28`, `M30`, `%`.\n- A diff of `examples/first-part.camproj` against a run with the good file shows the damage:\n  - The header changes from `O0001 (VMC 3-AXIS)` to `O0001 (CAMCRAFT)`.\n  - All three `M8` lines and all three `M9` lines are gone. The program cuts with no coolant.\n  - The motion lines are the same. The program looks correct.\n\nAfter the fix, the CLI exits 1, writes no file, and gives this message:\n\n`post blocked - the default machine file 3axis-vmc.mch cannot be read (default machine: 3axis-vmc.mch in <dir>\\assets\\machines: The system cannot find the file specified. (os error 2)) - mount a machine on the setup, or reinstall the file`\n\nA malformed file gives `post blocked - the default machine file 3axis-vmc.mch is malformed (<parse error>) - mount a machine on the setup, or reinstall the file`.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
